{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261030T014656Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "ca1531157f04f09eb5bea87f", "title": "[AINews] Gemini 4 Carbon tops leaderboards, launches for cyber defenders", "url": "https://latent.space/p/ainews-gemini-4-carbon/", "source": "Latent Space", "published": "2026-10-29T05:55:19+00:00", "is_ai": 0.99, "worthiness": 0.7375, "worthiness_confidence": 0.87, "final_score": 0.7375, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "feed_full_text", "text_chars": 37099, "delivered": true, "summary": "Google DeepMind launched Gemini 4 Carbon, a frontier model topping independent benchmarks with 59 on Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index v5, scoring 88.2% on SEC-bench Pro for cybersecurity. Carbon features a 1M-token context window, costs $2/$10 per million input/output tokens with 50% launch discount, and initially rolls out only to cyber defenders via the Fairwind Program. The model leads on coding and agentic tasks but trails Opus 5.5 on some benchmarks. Key takeaway: Carbon's cybersecurity focus and strong performance on long-horizon tasks make it valuable for security teams, though limited availability and hallucination rates (11%, up from Argon's 4%) warrant caution in deployment.", "jev_ms": 241.1, "jev_input_tokens": 9925, "jev_cost": 0.00041685, "llm_ms": 3078.0, "llm_cost": 0.011041, "errors": []}
