{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261030T014656Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "b6b30743068c26272d898fb0", "title": "Welcome Le Chonk: Mistral Large 4 on Hugging Face", "url": "https://huggingface.co/blog/mistral-large4", "source": "Hugging Face - Blog", "published": "2026-10-29T00:00:00+00:00", "is_ai": 0.99, "worthiness": 0.765, "worthiness_confidence": 0.95, "final_score": 0.765, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 16318, "delivered": true, "summary": "Mistral Large 4 (Le Chonk) is a 1T-parameter multimodal MoE model with 49B active parameters and 1M context window, combining sparse attention with a Pixtral vision encoder. It excels in cybersecurity (82% on vulnerability reproduction-and-patch tasks), coding (49.8% Coding Agent Index), and multimodal understanding. The model ships with day-zero support for transformers, vLLM, and llama.cpp, plus TRL fine-tuning capabilities. Key takeaway: open-weight architecture enables custom security systems on proprietary codebases while maintaining higher refusal rates than other open models on jailbreak benchmarks.", "jev_ms": 185.0, "jev_input_tokens": 4800, "jev_cost": 0.0002016, "llm_ms": 2436.8, "llm_cost": 0.005659, "errors": []}
{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261030T014656Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "6394645bd5105adc5435eb92", "title": "Introducing AnySpeechRecognizer and AnyDecisionModel: Open Models for Speech and Decisions on Apple Platforms", "url": "https://huggingface.co/blog/anydecisionmodel", "source": "Hugging Face - Blog", "published": "2026-10-29T00:00:00+00:00", "is_ai": 0.99, "worthiness": 0.7575, "worthiness_confidence": 0.97, "final_score": 0.7575, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 16543, "delivered": true, "summary": "Hugging Face released AnySpeechRecognizer and AnyDecisionModel, two Swift packages for running specialized models on Apple devices. AnySpeechRecognizer provides speech-to-text with pluggable engines including NVIDIA's Parakeet v3 (1.55% WER on LibriSpeech test-clean) and Alibaba's Qwen3-ASR, plus speaker diarization via NVIDIA's Sortformer. AnyDecisionModel answers typed questions by extracting probabilities from language models or decision heads like Cloudflare's Clef-Flash, avoiding text parsing. Both download open models from Hugging Face Hub and run locally on Core ML or MLX, letting builders replace Apple's default engines while keeping familiar APIs.", "jev_ms": 139.0, "jev_input_tokens": 4947, "jev_cost": 0.000207774, "llm_ms": 2364.6, "llm_cost": 0.005771, "errors": []}
