{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261030T014656Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "37f6c0c263213efdb83de3ed", "title": "Day 0 support for Mistral Large 4 on vLLM", "url": "https://vllm.ai/blog/2026-10-29-mistral-large-4", "source": "vLLM Blog", "published": "2026-10-29T00:00:00+00:00", "is_ai": 0.99, "worthiness": 0.99, "worthiness_confidence": 0.97, "final_score": 0.99, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 27382, "delivered": true, "summary": "vLLM shipped day-0 support for Mistral Large 4, a 1-trillion-parameter sparse MoE multimodal model with novel architecture features (MLA attention, DSA sparse indexing, cross-layer KV sharing, NoPE layers). The implementation required significant infrastructure work: breakable CUDA graphs, decode/prefill context parallelism optimizations reducing DCP overhead from 7ms to 3.2ms per step, DSpark speculative decoding achieving 2.85x acceptance length, and HiSparse host-memory KV offload enabling 4.5–5.7x capacity. Supporting ML4 across NVIDIA, AMD, and TPU platforms involved hand-written fusions, disaggregated serving with NIXL, and MXFP4 expert quantization. The key takeaway: sparse attention enables efficient long-context serving when combined with careful memory management and platform-specific optimizations.", "jev_ms": 155.2, "jev_input_tokens": 8933, "jev_cost": 0.000375186, "llm_ms": 3741.5, "llm_cost": 0.010518, "errors": []}
